{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2316 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "30e7a8a699fc8e8ab19b93acae9957e04ed462a667586bb9c416511109a9f183" :edb/db-before-t 2315 :edb/db-after-t 2316 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535628 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:56:17.186Z" 13194139535628 true] [17592186147381 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358217 13194139535628 true] [17592186147382 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358224 13194139535628 true] [17592186147382 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358231 13194139535628 true] [17592186147382 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358238 13194139535628 true] [17592186148109 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535628 true] [17592186148109 1100 "Let $y = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)a_{n}x^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $y^{″} - y = 0$. Find $f(n)$, given that the recurrence relation for $a_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$a_{n + 2} = (a_{n})/(f(n)), n = 0, 1, 2…$" 13194139535628 false] [17592186148109 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186148109 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=(n+1)(n+2).$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358218 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1089 "q-101389" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $18{y}^{″}-9y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1113 #uuid "b5bd1188-011f-5de8-8224-47cb9fd29c4b" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358217 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[18(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-9{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n18(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-9{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{2(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=2(n+1)(n+2).$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358219 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358220 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358221 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358222 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358223 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1041 "selection" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358223 13194139535628 true] [17592186358218 1110 #uuid "ccc29b0b-638a-5b35-a5d4-a57711a38aac" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358219 1034 "f(n)=-2(n+1)(n+2)" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358219 1111 #uuid "1602d4cf-6f96-55a1-9aa5-af0e750fffaa" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358220 1034 "f(n)=-\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358220 1111 #uuid "563dbd2e-ece6-50cd-9efb-c52e41d8e252" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358221 1034 "f(n)=\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358221 1111 #uuid "1b33b297-5e39-5b84-9c11-20bad5561b7a" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358222 1034 "f(n)=2n(n+1)" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358222 1111 #uuid "151db3f9-258e-5d5b-b887-b6ace8346d3e" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358223 1034 "f(n)=2(n+1)(n+2)" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358223 1111 #uuid "4799e5ad-19e2-55fc-8842-686df215e6b6" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358225 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1089 "q-101403" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $5{y}^{′}-2xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1113 #uuid "b4a15be5-56fd-581a-a9cd-9c8be7b9791e" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358224 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-2x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }5(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }5(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }5(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[5(n+1){a}_{n+1}-2{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,5(n+1){a}_{n+1}=2{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358226 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358227 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358228 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358229 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358230 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1041 "selection" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358228 13194139535628 true] [17592186358225 1110 #uuid "6e663ad7-1dab-574f-a964-40d082646d40" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358226 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{5{a}_{n}}{2(n+1)}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358226 1111 #uuid "050a1396-0a09-55cb-96b9-e4be221a86fd" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358227 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=10{a}_{n}(n+1)" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358227 1111 #uuid "6b8f18fc-83b2-5020-93c4-f82f0a57f697" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358228 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358228 1111 #uuid "3303e07a-ba8e-5b03-b423-d30ca1b4908a" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358229 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358229 1111 #uuid "badd6234-c1a5-5521-8a70-271e206dd05c" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358230 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{5n+2}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358230 1111 #uuid "234f91be-a0ab-557d-9ca2-cde2074029b0" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358232 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1089 "q-102315" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $xy+9{y}^{′}=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1113 #uuid "9acbfa33-35c8-5eb4-af30-be51fe0a0220" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358231 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+9{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }9(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }9(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }9(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+9{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n9{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[{a}_{n-1}+9(n+1){a}_{n+1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,9(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358233 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358234 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358235 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358236 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358237 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1041 "selection" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358236 13194139535628 true] [17592186358232 1110 #uuid "fdae2540-94a1-5d66-8c47-0d41668d85d7" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358233 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358233 1111 #uuid "4ab77680-db2f-5819-961b-2d868d057602" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358234 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9n+1}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358234 1111 #uuid "3a067f6b-3a66-577b-987e-a04ed4cd85ed" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358235 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=-9{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358235 1111 #uuid "0abd4e93-6c73-5a00-b2f1-3b79c4965074" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358236 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358236 1111 #uuid "2155f10e-a88d-5885-8ceb-f8baa45f3603" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358237 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9n+1}" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535628 true] [17592186358237 1111 #uuid "ad71331c-fca7-592e-9d2c-7ad49bd3901c" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358239 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1089 "q-365776" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{′}+2xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3…$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1113 #uuid "01e4a118-39ab-5f83-a84a-4e3bea205b9e" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358238 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+2x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}+2{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{-2{a}_{n-1}}{n+1},\\,n=1,2,3….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" 13194139535628 true] [17592186358239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358240 13194139535628 true] [17592186358239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358241 13194139535628 true] [17592186358239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358242 13194139535628 true] [17592186358239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358243 13194139535628 true] [17592186358239 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358244 13194139535628 true] [1759218635